    connections:
      "Ten ideas, one organizing principle: in Sweden, the statute very often sets the floor and the procedure, while the real substantive content gets filled in by a kollektivavtal the state deliberately stays out of negotiating itself. Saklig grund and turordning establish the basic architecture of lawful dismissal, a last-resort standard for personal grounds and a seniority-based, recently loosened selection rule for redundancies, while uppsägningstid and the varsel obligation then layer the individual notice period and the separate, state-facing labor-market notification duty on top of that basic dismissal analysis. Den svenska modellen and MBL explain the structure underneath everything else in this lecture: wages and most substantive conditions negotiated directly between unions and employers, a genuine pre-decision duty to negotiate significant changes, and a peace obligation that gives both sides a reason to actually reach an agreement rather than fight indefinitely. Konflikträtt then shows exactly where that peace obligation's limits lie, concentrating real strike leverage around the negotiation of a new agreement rather than leaving it available at any time. Diskrimineringslagen and föräldraledighetslagen return the focus to the individual employee, one through a genuinely proactive, complaint-independent compliance duty, the other through a leave-protection framework that folds directly back into the saklig grund standard the moment a leave-related motive taints a dismissal. Arbetsmiljölagen closes the individual-protection thread with the skyddsombud's remarkable, independent power to halt dangerous work on the spot, and övergång av verksamhet closes the lecture by testing the whole system against a business transfer, carrying terms forward automatically while, unlike several neighboring systems, giving the individual employee a genuine right to object, the clearest single illustration in this lecture of how consistently Swedish labor law builds real, usable agency for both unions and individual workers into a framework the state otherwise leaves largely to the parties themselves.",
